WEBVTT

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.480
Shigeno

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.500
<i>In a game-ending situation like that,
 the catcher should never leave the plate.</i>

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.030
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.610
<i>I should've left it for Hikaru.</i>

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.270
You sure look glum.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.350
Hikaru?!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.950
Are you okay now?

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.820
Why wouldn't I be?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.590
Is that some sort of joke?

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.870
You had to be taken away in an ambulance
after our collision yesterday!

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.940
Oh, that? Nah, I'm totally fine.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.240
But forget that. I want you 
to catch for me, Daigo-kun.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.880
We could've won yesterday's game,
but we gave up a walk-off hit.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.130
We need to practice some more.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.430
S-So you're sure you're okay?
If you are, that's a big relief.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.690
Oh, but you should 
probably take it easy today.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.880
You pitched in a game yesterday, after all.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.400
It's all good.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.650
But your arm must be tired.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.080
I just said it's all good.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.900
Anyway, whose fault do you 
think it was that we lost?

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.560
If you hadn't gotten in my way,
we would've taken the game to extra innings.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.920
And I wouldn't have had to die.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.500
<i>It... It was a dream...</i>

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:38.820
No way...!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.480
Oh, good morning, Daigo.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.710
Morning.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.450
It's already eleven.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.910
You sure slept in.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:45.970
Yeah.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.080
I had trouble getting to sleep last night.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:53.670
Here you go.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.370
What?

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.730
Manager Tashiro told me you needed to 
give him a call as soon as you woke up.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.840
Hey, Daigo!

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.910
<i>Good job out there yesterday.</i>

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.800
Um, Hikaru...

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.810
How's Hikaru doing?

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.670
<i>Satou-san called me this morning.</i>

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.560
<i>Hikaru was knocked out cold 
and suffered a concussion,</i>

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.290
<i>but I hear he's doing better already.</i>

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.820
Really?

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.250
<i>Yeah. So no need to worry.</i>

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.070
What a relief!

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.100
Thanks to you guys,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.290
the last tournament for the sixth 
graders ended in one hell of a game.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.830
Thank you.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.210
<i>O-Oh, no, I didn't do anything special.</i>

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.660
<i>And anyway, we didn't even beat Touto.</i>

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.520
And that's fine.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.090
Just getting the chance to play Touto
was something special in itself.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:50.030
Not only that, you guys gave them a real 
run for their money, which is amazing.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.110
Manager... Thank you very much!

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.690
Use this as an incentive.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.590
You need to keep going with 
baseball in middle school.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.500
Yes, sir!

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.120
Home 
Run

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.160
So Hikaru-kun's okay?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.500
That's great news.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.440
I know, right?

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.950
I couldn't sleep last night.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.760
I was worried about Hikaru,
and I'm the reason we lost the game.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.030
But it wasn't your fault.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.930
Remember what the manager said?

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.020
We all fought hard,
 and it was a great game.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.560
Even so, I really want to go see Hikaru 
as soon as I can and apologize to him.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.190
Why don't you call him, then?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.200
Or if you know his address, we could go to 
his house next Sunday. That'd surprise him!

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.700
B-But he lives in Gunma!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.550
We're in grade school. We can't 
take the train that far on our own.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.770
"That far"? It's still in the Kantou region.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.460
I think it's only about two hours by train.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.380
Sorry, Dad.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.810
It wasn't my intention to get you to 
drive us somewhere on your day off.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.980
When you said you wanted to go 
all the way to Gunma with a boy,

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.670
your dear old dad just 
<i>had </i>to get in on the action.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.010
Right, Shigeno-kun?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.560
Y-Yessir!

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.760
My mom was also okay with this arrangement.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.060
Takazaki

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.050
I guess this is it.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.800
Sakaguchi

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:54.760
The GPS says we're here, 
but that doesn't say Satou.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.810
I think Sakaguchi's right.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.810
It's Hikaru's mother's maiden name.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.440
Oh, I see.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.510
I guess they're not in.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.340
Didn't I say this might happen?

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.710
I said: "What if they're 
not in when we get there?"

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.120
Normally, you call someone first.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.390
We wanted to surprise him, though!

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.960
Oh, well.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.090
Their car's here, though,
so I guess we should wait a while.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.700
Satou-san!

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.470
Daigo-kun.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.890
What are you guys doing here?

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.210
We wanted to see Hikaru!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:48.650
I never got a chance to talk to him 
after we lost that game.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.420
We're so glad you're here!

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.040
So where's Hikaru-kun? 
Did he go out somewhere?

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.950
When is he coming back?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.970
Hikaru's...

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.330
Hikaru's...

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.330
...not coming back.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:05.400
Huh?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.820
I'm sorry, but you can't see him today.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.180
You should head on home.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.640
What?

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.600
Wh-What do you mean, we can't see him?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.810
They said he had a concussion,
but he was fine!

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:29.670
I wanted to wait until we had 
a clearer picture before talking to you,

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.020
but I guess I can't leave you in the dark.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.990
Hikaru regained consciousness, 
but he still can't move.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.370
When you two ran into each other,
his neck took the brunt of the impact.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.790
He was transferred to 
a local hospital today.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:53.100
I'm here to pick up a few of his things.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.940
Unfortunately, only family 
members are allowed to visit him.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.010
B-But that's...

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.720
He <i>will</i> get better, though, won't he?

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:06.330
We don't know.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.480
He can't move anything below his neck,

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.050
so we don't know what'll happen.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.770
N-No...

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.180
<i>No way!</i>

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:48.500
Shall we pull into a rest stop 
and grab a nice bite to eat?

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.000
S-Sure.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.880
Mifune Elementary School

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.740
<i>Shigeno-kun...</i>

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.400
<i>It's been two months since that day...</i>

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.000
Daigo, are you home?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.690
Good one, Nagai!

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.360
Keep running!

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:20.370
Bow!

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.240
Thank you!

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.830
You all did great over
these past three years.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:31.080
Today's farewell game was the last time the 
sixth graders got to wear these uniforms.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:33.730
Parting is always sad,

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:37.190
but you should be proud of what you did
 here, doggedly chasing that white ball,

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.090
and you must keep 
working hard in the future!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.390
Yes, sir!

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.390
Last but not least, Coach Fujii and I

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:46.510
have a parting gift for each of you.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:50.730
We got you all some really rare 
items from a famous local store!

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.480
When I call your name, please come forward.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.820
Number one, shortstop, Kimura!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:56.630
Yes, sir!

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.490
Good work.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.210
Thank you very much!

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.560
Number two, center field, Nagai.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:06.450
Yes, sir!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.930
Number three, pitcher, Urabe.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:09.610
Yes, sir!

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.440
Number four, catcher, Andy.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.240
Yes, sir!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.780
Number five, third base, Ariyoshi!

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:16.710
Yes, sir!

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.240
Number six, left field, Kishimoto.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.010
Yes, sir!

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.520
Number seven, first base,  Matsubara.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:23.510
Yes, sir!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.000
Number eight, second base, Katsumata.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.010
Yes, sir!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.510
Number nine, right field, Sakura.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:30.310
Yes, sir!

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.420
These are so cute!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.150
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:43.280
Heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:47.000
Thank you so much!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.790
So I guess we'll drop Andy 
and Urabe off on the way.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:56.960
Yeah, thank you.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:58.570
Off we go!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:15.940
So I guess Daigo didn't show up.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:18.650
Yeah.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:21.990
I've tried talking to him 
about it a number of times,

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.560
but he's convinced himself that 
the accident was all his fault.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.740
He's shut himself off from the world.

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:31.770
Apparently, he even said
he's never playing baseball again.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.360
Is he for real?

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:38.500
And how's Satou doing since the accident?

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.480
I haven't heard anything.

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:43.480
Or rather, I don't have the heart to ask.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.320
They're only letting relatives see him.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.600
Satou-san has asked me to leave 
them alone for the time being.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:54.090
He says he understands 
it was an unfortunate accident,

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.420
and well, he doesn't want us 
worrying about them.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.320
Here, Daigo.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.100
It's from the Dolphins' manager, Tashiro.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:13.520
It was today, wasn't it?

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.050
The Dolphins' farewell game 
for the sixth graders.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:17.960
Yeah.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:22.080
That's the commemorative gift. 
All the sixth graders got the same thing.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:28.700
You could've at least said 
goodbye to your teammates.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:31.610
Can't we just drop it? It's over now.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.220
Besides, it was probably better this way.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:38.310
If this emo kid had showed up,
he would've brought the whole mood down.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.730
It's just tiresome.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.750
Shut up.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.560
My baseball-playing days ended 
at the summer tournament.

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:50.990
Thanks for the food. Good night.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.120
Uh, um, yeah. Good night.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.280
What's wrong with that kid?

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:02.930
He doesn't even really talk anymore.

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:04.960
How long's he going to stay like this?

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.970
It's not surprising, after what happened.

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:13.140
I hoped it would get 
better with time, though.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:20.770
For better or worse, everything's
 either black or white to him.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.480
You mean everything's
"baseball or not" to him.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.980
He sees everything in terms of baseball.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.790
You're right.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.150
He's like your pop in that way.

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.990
He gets his stubbornness from him, too.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.470
Oh, a message.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:40.750
I wonder if it's Kasumi...

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:43.330
Mom!

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.520
Speak of the devil! Look!

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.190
Now that's something!

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.510
Big Daddy

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.510
I'm coming home tomorrow. 
Please let your mom know.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.500
Sir? Sir?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:04.690
I'm sorry to disturb you,

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.570
but we've landed at Haneda.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.990
Oh, really?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.520
Thank you.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.890
It's been six months 
since I was last in Japan.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.660
I wonder if my kids have grown taller again.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:34.090
Shigeno Izumi-san, 4m 62cm.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.090
Fuurin Academy Private Middle School

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.210
Great jump, Izumi.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.350
Maybe you should do track 
and field in high school?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.510
Oh, stop it.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:45.230
I've decided to apply to Yokohama Seirin 
because they have a girls' baseball team.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.570
Wow, really?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.420
Yeah.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.730
Looks like I'm not ready 
to give up baseball just yet.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:55.610
So you're going to leave, 
even though Fuurin has a high school?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.490
Yeah...

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:57.680
Sir!

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:58.420
Hm?

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.830
There's a strange guy over there.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.530
What?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.540
Look, over there!

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:06.040
He's been watching us this whole time.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.250
It's some weirdo, sir!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.610
I bet it's that pervert who's been 
seen in the area a lot recently!

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.660
What did you say?!

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:14.820
Ew.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:16.050
I'm scared!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.830
Hi! Izumi!

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.630
Th-That's...

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:23.810
The pervert's waving at us!

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.810
Okay! You girls wait here.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.690
Hey, you over there!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.020
Hey!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.340
Stop!

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.530
<i>Why is he running away?</i>

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.520
Shigeno-kun!

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:00.370
So our teacher said earlier

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:03.590
that you were also trying 
to get into Fuurin Academy.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.480
Yeah. I'm going to give it a try.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.800
No idea if I'll get in, though.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.900
Jeez, why didn't you say something?

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:16.120
I told you I was applying to Fuurin ages ago.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.310
You did?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:26.390
Oh, yeah, your older sister 
goes to Fuurin, doesn't she?

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.440
Yeah.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:32.170
And she's captain of the baseball team.

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.550
It's her third year, 
so she already left the team.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.520
She won't be there by the 
time we get there, anyway.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.700
Really?

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:42.030
That's too bad.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:45.540
It would've been reassuring to 
have an older girl on the team.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.690
I hope there are some other 
girls on the team, though.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.250
You're joining... the baseball team?

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:58.350
Yes, of course.

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:00.320
Playing baseball is a lot of fun.

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:03.750
I see.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:12.970
You have to snap out of this!

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:16.280
You need to go back to 
being the old Shigeno-kun!

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.420
I want to play baseball with you again!

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:25.710
That game... What happened to 
Hikaru-kun wasn't your fault,

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:31.600
and I bet it'd break Hikaru-kun's 
heart to see you like this.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:37.530
I also... don't want you to hate baseball.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:40.500
I can't do it.

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:47.040
You were there, too. 
That time we were in Gunma.

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:48.670
In Gunma?

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.310
It was so far away.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:58.730
Hikaru came all that way for our games.

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:06.970
And he must've woken up really early
every time we had a morning game.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:09.970
How much do you have 
to love baseball to do that?

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:16.520
And then... I...

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:19.620
Shigeno-kun... Then—

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:21.260
I just told you, I can't!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.390
Don't talk about it!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:27.700
Never mention baseball 
or Hikaru to me ever again!

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:33.580
Whatever happens... 
I'll never play baseball again!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.180
Shigeno-kun!

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:43.560
<i>Hikaru's... paralyzed 
for the rest of his life.</i>

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:47.570
<i>How can I even go out on the 
field like it didn't happen?!</i>

00:21:05.210 --> 00:21:06.200
Yo!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.780
What's up, Daigo?

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:09.990
P-Pop?

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.500
<i>Shigeno-kun's dad?</i>

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.410
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.770
What do you mean?

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.170
The season ended yesterday, so I came home.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.260
Didn't anybody tell you?

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:26.760
When I got home, your mom was out, 
and no one else was there.

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:30.760
So I went to Izumi's school 
to watch her class,

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.270
and now, I've come to pick you up.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.820
You been keeping well, Daigo?

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:43.500
Y-Yeah...

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:48.660
<i>Huh? Why?</i>

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:52.250
<i>Why am I crying?</i>

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.610
H-Hey! Daigo?

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:04.840
<i>I don't know why tears 
started streaming down my face.</i>

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.670
<i>But... what I </i>do<i> know is, 
I don't want Pop to see me cry.</i>

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:17.970
So you want a race back to the house?

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:19.590
Fine by me!

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:21.490
Don't underestimate me!

00:22:21.490 --> 00:22:24.070
You kids ain't gonna beat me just yet!

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:01.410
Why?

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:05.000
Why did you have to come home <i>now</i>?

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:08.220
I poured my heart and soul into baseball.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:12.680
I wanted to show you too, but it's over now.

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:16.180
But you know something? 
In truth...

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:17.900
In truth, I...

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
The Promise

00:24:18.820 --> 00:24:20.800
Next time: "The Promise."

00:24:21.210 --> 00:24:23.290
Run to the stage of your dreams!
